Round every NCollection_IncAllocator allocation up to 8 bytes.

OCCT 8.0.1 bump-allocates the requested size unrounded, so after an allocation of 4 bytes (for
example the edge orientations of a wire with one edge) every later object in the block, such as
BRepMesh's faces, sits at an address that is not 8-byte aligned. 7.6 rounded the size.
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops on the first such object. Mesh2Cad ADR-027.

